WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.721 --> 00:00:14.823
Zann landed in a puddle of swampy water.

2
00:00:15.203 --> 00:00:16.584
"Drat," he muttered.

3
00:00:17.244 --> 00:00:20.466
His Conveyance teacher was always scolding him for this sort of thing.

4
00:00:21.206 --> 00:00:24.308
Being a Red, Zann could zap himself far—and fast.

5
00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:26.669
But his focus still needed some work.

6
00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:28.490
That didn't matter now though.

7
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:29.671
He was out of the house.

8
00:00:29.971 --> 00:00:31.332
It was time to find Darb.

9
00:00:32.128 --> 00:00:36.811
Pursing his lips, he whistled, trying to imitate the call of a lesser swamp swift.

10
00:00:37.992 --> 00:00:41.074
"Not bad," a voice said from the grassy hillock behind him.

11
00:00:41.094 --> 00:00:43.796
"I always knew you had talents other than magic."

12
00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.038
Zann spun around and grinned.

13
00:00:46.058 --> 00:00:48.700
"Hey, Darb," he said, stepping out of the water.

14
00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:50.221
"Sorry I'm late.

15
00:00:50.461 --> 00:00:51.982
Boz didn't want me to go out."

16
00:00:52.002 --> 00:00:54.964
"Because of the warning about Reds disappearing?"

17
00:00:55.224 --> 00:00:56.365
Darb asked thoughtfully.

18
00:00:56.385 --> 00:00:58.106
"I've been hearing about that."

19
00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:04.043
Darb was a Void, one of a small group of people in Magica born without any magical abilities.

20
00:01:04.723 --> 00:01:07.145
That was the reason he and Zann had met in the first place.

21
00:01:07.845 --> 00:01:12.849
On Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School, he'd encountered Jev and his friends teasing Darb.

22
00:01:13.489 --> 00:01:14.650
Zann had told them to stop.

23
00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.531
"Who's going to make me?"

24
00:01:16.851 --> 00:01:17.592
Jev had sneered.

25
00:01:17.612 --> 00:01:21.655
"That red hair of yours doesn't mean you get to tell me what to do."

26
00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:25.317
Then he'd turned and shoved Darb into the wall—hard.

27
00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:29.140
Looking back, Zann knew he probably should have called a teacher.

28
00:01:29.908 --> 00:01:34.812
Instead he'd acted on impulse, rubbing his fingers together until sparks began to jump from his hand.

29
00:01:35.712 --> 00:01:39.715
Jev didn’t even know what had happened until his friends started snickering and pointing at him.

30
00:01:40.936 --> 00:01:43.638
Zann had given him a pair of oversized donkey ears.

31
00:01:44.338 --> 00:01:46.640
It took Jev several tries to undo the spell.

32
00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:51.583
Ever since then Jev had been Zann's enemy, and Darb had been Zann's friend.

33
00:01:52.304 --> 00:01:53.805
Darb didn't attend school anymore.

34
00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:57.788
Voids were only required to study the basics of theory and history.

35
00:01:58.544 --> 00:02:03.588
Once classes started doing practical magic lessons, Voids usually dropped out and studied on their own.

36
00:02:04.649 --> 00:02:12.034
Most ended up finding careers as companions, greeters, animal caretakers, and mediators, or other jobs that required no

37
00:02:12.114 --> 00:02:16.917
magic. Most people in Magica would never purposely discriminate against a Void.

38
00:02:17.598 --> 00:02:21.360
But Zann had noticed that people said things in front of Darb that they wouldn't say in front

39
00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:21.761
of others.

40
00:02:22.481 --> 00:02:26.044
It was as if they thought Voids were deaf and dumb as well as lacking magic.

41
00:02:26.976 --> 00:02:28.397
That didn't seem fair to Zann.

42
00:02:28.617 --> 00:02:31.159
But it did allow Darb to hear a lot of interesting gossip.

43
00:02:31.179 --> 00:02:33.240
"What have you heard about the warning?"

44
00:02:33.661 --> 00:02:34.801
Zann asked his friend now.

45
00:02:34.821 --> 00:02:36.903
"Not much," Darb said.

46
00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:39.705
"Everyone's talking about the message from the palace though.

47
00:02:40.385 --> 00:02:44.768
The mayor is so nervous that she put a Shield spell over the entire town hall."

48
00:02:44.788 --> 00:02:47.330
"Boz is trying to find out more.

49
00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:50.652
In the meantime he wants me to stay inside."

50
00:02:51.152 --> 00:02:52.153
Zann rolled his eyes.

51
00:02:52.173 --> 00:02:56.176
"You can't blame him for being worried after what happened to your parents."

52
00:02:57.092 --> 00:02:57.633
"I guess."

53
00:02:58.033 --> 00:02:59.854
Zann jumped onto a larger hillock.

54
00:02:59.874 --> 00:03:01.716
"So what have you been doing?"

55
00:03:02.456 --> 00:03:03.277
"Studying insects."

56
00:03:03.297 --> 00:03:05.279
"Insects, huh?"

57
00:03:05.639 --> 00:03:06.139
Zann said.

58
00:03:06.159 --> 00:03:08.822
"Why not study something more exciting?

59
00:03:09.142 --> 00:03:10.143
Dragons, maybe?"

60
00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:12.865
"Speaking of dragons, where's Zing?"

61
00:03:13.145 --> 00:03:13.725
Darb asked.

62
00:03:13.745 --> 00:03:16.328
"He was outside when I left.

63
00:03:16.648 --> 00:03:18.549
I couldn't get him without Boz seeing me."

64
00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.351
Darb looked disappointed.

65
00:03:20.671 --> 00:03:23.753
Everyone assumed he'd end up being an animal caretaker someday.

66
00:03:24.414 --> 00:03:26.636
He loved animals of all kinds, and they loved him.

67
00:03:27.344 --> 00:03:30.125
Zing broke into a happy whistling song whenever he saw him.

68
00:03:30.986 --> 00:03:32.946
Darb stepped toward a slow-moving stream.

69
00:03:33.627 --> 00:03:34.887
"Look, panic bugs."

70
00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:36.748
He leaned closer for a better look.

71
00:03:36.768 --> 00:03:38.749
"Can you get a picture of them for me?"

72
00:03:39.709 --> 00:03:43.591
"Sure." Zann rubbed his hands together and stared at the shiny red bugs.

73
00:03:44.251 --> 00:03:47.772
Blink! A piece of paper appeared and fluttered to the swampy ground.

74
00:03:48.493 --> 00:03:49.193
Zann picked it up.

75
00:03:49.493 --> 00:03:52.194
The image of the panic bugs was there in full color.

76
00:03:52.214 --> 00:03:56.956
"Thanks." Darb took the blink image, folded it, and put it into his pocket.

77
00:03:57.980 --> 00:04:02.684
Then he gently scooped up the bugs and put them in his other pocket, being careful not to

78
00:04:02.744 --> 00:04:04.446
startle them into releasing their stink.

79
00:04:05.146 --> 00:04:06.327
"Want to help me look for leeches?"

80
00:04:06.708 --> 00:04:07.108
he asked.

81
00:04:07.128 --> 00:04:09.110
"I've seen them around here before."

82
00:04:09.130 --> 00:04:11.572
"Leeches?" Zann echoed.

83
00:04:11.592 --> 00:04:14.394
"Why?" "I've been reading about them.

84
00:04:14.735 --> 00:04:17.597
It's fascinating how they can suck the magic out of people."

85
00:04:17.617 --> 00:04:20.019
"Yeah." Zann grinned.

86
00:04:20.039 --> 00:04:25.064
"Back in First City, my friends and I used to stick them on each other as a joke.

87
00:04:25.796 --> 00:04:30.078
It would take about a million of them to drain enough magic to make a difference, but it

88
00:04:30.118 --> 00:04:30.878
was still funny."

89
00:04:31.758 --> 00:04:34.059
Darb peered into the water's murky depths.

90
00:04:34.079 --> 00:04:36.901
"Leeches are very shy," he said.

91
00:04:36.921 --> 00:04:39.121
"They live at the bottom of streams like this.

92
00:04:39.462 --> 00:04:41.883
We'll have to be quiet and feel around in the water."

93
00:04:41.903 --> 00:04:43.763
"Why go to all that trouble?"

94
00:04:44.143 --> 00:04:45.544
Zann rubbed his fingers together.

95
00:04:45.564 --> 00:04:47.765
"I'll displace the water.

96
00:04:48.305 --> 00:04:50.546
Then you can grab as many leeches as you want."

97
00:04:50.566 --> 00:04:52.167
"Zann, wait!"

98
00:04:52.487 --> 00:04:53.127
Darb began.

99
00:04:53.147 --> 00:04:55.048
"That won't—" Shloop!

100
00:04:55.756 --> 00:05:00.019
The water in the nearest section of the stream levitated, hanging as droplets in the air.

101
00:05:00.739 --> 00:05:05.222
Several fish and other creatures were left lying on the bottom of the streambed, looking confused.

102
00:05:05.242 --> 00:05:08.344
"Leeches!" Zann cried, pointing.

103
00:05:09.005 --> 00:05:13.528
Almost before he spotted them, the slimy little creatures had burrowed into the soft sand.

104
00:05:13.548 --> 00:05:15.609
"Oh. They're gone."

105
00:05:15.629 --> 00:05:19.592
"I tried to tell you that," Darb said with a sigh.

106
00:05:19.612 --> 00:05:23.034
"They dive away from air unless they're latched on to someone."

107
00:05:23.054 --> 00:05:25.376
"Sorry," Zann said.

108
00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:27.601
"Hey, did you hear that?"

109
00:05:28.502 --> 00:05:28.982
"Hear what?"

110
00:05:29.843 --> 00:05:31.445
Zann tilted his head, listening.

111
00:05:31.465 --> 00:05:33.686
"That buzzing noise," he said.

112
00:05:33.706 --> 00:05:42.594
"Sounds like an irritated spy fly, or maybe—" A loud, angry buzzing drowned out his words.

113
00:05:43.395 --> 00:05:48.219
Suddenly a whole swarm of tiny, glittering dragons came zipping out of a hole in the bank and

114
00:05:48.259 --> 00:05:49.240
started stinging him!
